WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.150
- I would like you, as a talk show host,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.981
to introduce our next guest.

00:00:06.981 --> 00:00:08.960
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.985
- Okay great.

00:00:09.985 --> 00:00:14.500
He played the Coleslaw King of The world

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.884
and Josie's brother, Rob.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:18.833
Take a look.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:24.093
- I am Josie Geller high school
student, senior class, 1999.

00:00:25.836 --> 00:00:28.350
- Huh uh.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.030
You're kidding, right?

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.863
- What?

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.490
- Josie, do you remember high school?

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.200
- It was a long time ago.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.407
- Do you remember what they
called you in high school?

00:00:38.407 --> 00:00:43.407
- [Kids] Josie Grossy, Josie
Grossy, Josie Grossy, Josie!

00:00:47.185 --> 00:00:48.970
- Josie Grossy.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.596
- Please welcome David Arquette.

00:00:51.596 --> 00:00:54.346
(crowd cheering)

00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:08.953
David.

00:01:08.953 --> 00:01:09.786
- Okay.

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:14.849
I feel like I'm being punked. (laughs)

00:01:14.849 --> 00:01:18.017
I was told we were all
gonna be wearing costumes.

00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:19.963
(everyone laughs)

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:20.963
- I love it.

00:01:22.253 --> 00:01:23.843
I love it.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.350
I love it.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.330
And I want to say that
David and I have had

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.910
a really long history.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.460
We grew up in the same neighborhood

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.260
right down the street from each other.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.000
What was it like to know
each other, be friends,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.580
and then get to play
brother and sister together?

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.640
- Yeah, it was, it was a dream come true.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.463
I mean, you put this
beautiful film together

00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:50.950
that was so heartfelt

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.890
and has stood the test of time.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.050
And now you're here and
you're doing your show

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.280
and I'm so glad that like,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.498
you get to see how much
the world loves you.

00:01:59.498 --> 00:02:02.498
'Cause I love you and the world loves you.

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:03.915
- I love you too.

00:02:05.405 --> 00:02:08.220
I have loved you my whole life, David.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.430
You know, one of the scenes that I think

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.760
really resonated with people

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.760
was having Rob tell Josie,
which we all needed to hear

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.230
at some point in our life,

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.310
you can't be held back anymore

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.920
by your own personal insecurities.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.209
And that's where the famous line comes in,

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:32.247
"I'm not Josie Grossy anymore!"

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.657
(audience cheers)

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.230
Because we need someone to see the thing

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.938
that we cannot see us for ourselves.

00:02:44.938 --> 00:02:47.521
(upbeat music)

